                                merge 24beb5f0). Layout's mouseUp calls a kant extern; firing is proved with a synthetic point and
                                no window. (Topics/forms, Events, moved here.)
    THE RESIZE (2026-11-06, 2026-11-10; G3 item 2, 2026-11-21)
                                a resize re-runs setFrame on a fresh deep copy at the frame given (percent stays, SEQ 622 R0). Since G3
                                (SEQ 730) frames are kept by form name in formFrames, for one run: redrawWindow keeps the window's frame,
                                then redraws (a resize, a click redraw); keepFrame alone is a close; setFrame reads and clears the entry
                                for a request naming no frame. layoutFrame and its listener are retired. The window holds its own frame;
                                utilities does not track open windows -- that is this topic's (Tony, 2026-11-21 R3). WAITING: a real
                                window's resize and close calling redrawWindow and keepFrame (frameStoreT, resizeT, resizeLightT).
